                <pb facs="0950" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/803: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-01T17:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 4,
                            11.25 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Federico Tinoco in Congress this afternoon asked its permission to leave the
                    country on account of illness but he said nothing about resignation. Every
                    indication a complete change in the government very soon. Joaquin said farewell
                    to the police this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
